.TH SDL_GL_CreateContext 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GL_CreateContext \- Create an OpenGL context for an OpenGL window, and make it current.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_GLContext SDL_GL_CreateContext(SDL_Window *window);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The OpenGL context will be created with the current states set through
.BR SDL_GL_SetAttribute ()\[char46]
.PP
The
.BR SDL_Window
specified must have been created with the
.BR SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL
flag, or context creation will fail\[char46]
.PP
Windows users new to OpenGL should note that, for historical reasons, GL functions added after OpenGL version 1\[char46]1 are not available by default\[char46] Those functions must be loaded at run-time, either with an OpenGL extension-handling library or with
.BR SDL_GL_GetProcAddress ()
and its related functions\[char46]
.PP

.BR SDL_GLContext
is opaque to the application\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I window
the window to associate with the context\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the OpenGL context associated with
.BR window
or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GL_DestroyContext (3),
.BR SDL_GL_MakeCurrent (3)
